=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_7f3a — Evening dinner at the dining table, dishes to sink by 21:00

Yuki is home by 17:30 on weekdays (she drives in from the office around 17:15–17:30). She spends roughly 17:30–18:30 in the kitchen preparing dinner—she was seen in the kitchen at 18:00 on day 0 (Tuesday). By 19:00–19:30 she has set the table and sits down to eat; she was seen in the dining room at 20:00 with her plate, glass, and water bottle at the dining table. Omar is still at his afternoon-to-night shift (out until ~23:00), so this is a solo dinner. By 22:00 Yuki has moved to the living room for TV or reading; her glass has been washed and is at the kitchen sink.

This document sets itself apart by pinning the *dinner window* (19:00–20:30) and the *post-dinner sink reset* (20:30–22:00) for Yuki's personal tableware and the water bottle. It predicts that on a weekday evening the plate, glass, and water bottle are at dining_table_d1, not in the cupboard, not at the entry hook, and not on a person. After the meal, the glass migrates to sink_k1. The water bottle, having been used at the table, ends up back at desk_o1 or the kitchen counter by 21:30.

Refutation: if Yuki's plate or glass is sighted at dining_table_d1 outside 18:30–21:00 on a weekday, or if the water bottle is at the dining table while she is in the living room (i.e., she left it there), this document is wrong. If Omar is seen eating at the dining table at 20:00 on a weekday (he would still be at work), the solo-dinner assumption breaks.

