=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_9c2b — Kitchen tools rest at the sink after cooking; the pot goes to the pantry

On a weekday, Yuki cooks dinner around 17:30–18:30. She uses the pan, cutting board, knife, and spatula at the counter or on the stove. After the meal (by ~20:00–20:30) she washes everything and places the wet tools at sink_k1, where they dry. The pot, being larger, goes back to pantry_shelf_k1. By 22:00 all these items are at the sink or pantry, not on a person, not at the counter, and not in the dishwasher (there is no dishwasher receptacle in this home).

This document explains the day-0 "worst objects" list: the mixture predicted ON_PERSON for the pan, knife, cutting board, and spatula at 20:00, but they were actually at sink_k1. The pot was predicted ON_PERSON but was at pantry_shelf_k1. The snack bowl was predicted at coffee_table_l1 but was at sink_k1 (washed after a pre-dinner snack).

It differs from p_c007 (which predicted the cutting board and pan at counter_k1 during 18–19:30) by asserting that by 20:00 they have already been washed and moved to the sink. The 18:00–19:00 window is the only time they are at the counter; after that, sink_k1.

Refutation: if the pan or knife is sighted at counter_k1 after 20:00 on a weekday (still dirty, not yet washed), the "washed by 20:00" timing is wrong. If the pot is at sink_k1 rather than pantry_shelf_k1, the storage location is wrong. If Omar is the one cooking (he is at work until 23:00 on weekdays, so this would be unusual), the whole single-cooker model breaks.

